required_documents:
Elix-Forms pre-evaluation for a second-cycle (master's) course with a foreign degree - scanned copies of:
a) foreign final or provisional university degree (bachelor);
b) list of completed exams / transcript of records / diploma supplement of that bachelor degree;
c) descriptions of single subjects / syllabus of the foreign bachelor degree;
d) valid passport;
e) updated curriculum vitae;
f) CIMEA Statements or Declaration of Value for the foreign bachelor degree*;
g) required English language certificate (B2 CEFR or equivalent)*;
plus the payment receipt for the €20.00 non-refundable pre-evaluation fee (PagoPA, or bank transfer in specific cases), which is uploaded as a step of the online procedure.

*Items (f) and (g) may be submitted after the online pre-evaluation, but both are required to complete final enrolment at UNIUD.

Qualification-recognition route (choose one): DECLARATION OF VALUE issued by the Italian Embassy/Consulate in the awarding country, OR CIMEA Statements requested online through the diplome platform (https://cimea-diplome.it, registration at https://mywallet.cimea-diplome.it). For degrees from the 55 Lisbon Recognition Convention signatory countries, the ARDI Statement of Correspondence can be downloaded from www.ardi.cimea.it, but the CIMEA Verification Statement must still be requested. These procedures verify eligibility only; they do not convert the foreign degree into an Italian one, and holding them does not itself affect the admission assessment.

Additional documents for non-EU residents on the Universitaly portal: valid passport; passport-sized photograph; first-cycle university degree (or final/provisional single-cycle master's); English language certificate at B2 or equivalent.

The programme microsite does not add any programme-specific document beyond the university-wide list; a motivation letter is required for the English-taught BACHELOR (Management & Business Analytics) but is not listed among the required documents for master's applicants.
